// Arabic text for the game (Options › Language › Game text in Arabic). Written by Command Center's contributors in
// Modern Standard Arabic, worded the way Syrian dubbing does: short, plain and familiar. The community patch's Arabic
// (TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch, GPL-3.0) served as a reference.
//
// Rules (CommandCenter.Tests checks them):
//  - "byEnglish": the game's English text exactly (with its '&') -> Arabic, for every label with that text, so a
//    unit reads the same for every general. "text": by label, for one place; it wins over "byEnglish".
//  - Plain Arabic in reading order. Command Center joins the letters, reverses each line for the game and adds the
//    button's hotkey as " (X)" at the end.
//  - No harakat, no tatweel, digits 0-9, no '&'.
//  - The values the game fills in (%d, %ls...) are written {1}, {2}... in the order of the English. Within a line a
//    later value comes first in Arabic: "%ls does not have the map %ls" is "الخريطة {2} غير موجودة عند {1}".
//  - Units keep their English names in Arabic letters (همفي، كروسيدر، أوفرلورد); buildings, upgrades, powers and
//    orders are translated.
//  - A line break is \n. Long texts are broken into lines by Command Center; their own line breaks stay.
//  - "added": labels Generals Online asks for that the game's table does not have.
